{
  "language_code": "en",
  "text": "Good morning everyone. Um, so today, uh, we're going to talk about, you know, a few things. Let's get settled first. … Here's the truth nobody tells you about waiting. Waiting is not wasting. God is working in the wait, even when you can't see it. … I remember the year everything stopped. I had sent forty applications and heard nothing back. Not one reply. I thought my life was on pause. But looking back, that was the year my faith grew up. … So, um, anyway, uh, where was I. Right. Let me check my notes here. Okay. … Why do we hate waiting so much? Because waiting feels like losing control. And control is the thing we trust more than God. That's the hard part. … Isaiah forty thirty one says they that wait upon the Lord shall renew their strength. Renew. Not lose. The wait is where your strength is rebuilt. … Three things to do while you wait. First, keep showing up. Second, keep serving someone else. Third, keep a record of what God has already done. … And, uh, you know, there's more I could say about that, but, um, we'll, we'll get to it another time maybe. … If you're in a season of waiting today, don't give up. Your waiting is not wasted. It is working. And the answer is closer than you think. … Let's pray. Thank you all for coming, and, uh, see you next week.",
